[{"id":"smq-year2-2.28-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>Show that the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2+x-4=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> may be arranged in to each of the following:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\sqrt{4-x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac4{x+1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2=4-x\\Rightarrow x=\\sqrt{4-x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2+x-4=x(x+1)-4=0\\Rightarrow x(x+1)=4\\Rightarrow x=\\frac4{x+1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.28-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>Show that the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^3+2x-5=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> may be arranged in to each of the following:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\sqrt[3]{5-2x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac5{x^2+2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^3=5-2x\\Rightarrow x=\\sqrt[3]{5-2x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^3+2x-5=x(x^2+2)-5=0\\Rightarrow x(x^2+2)=5\\Rightarrow x=\\frac5{x^2+2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.28-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=x^3-x^2-2x-3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> may be written in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\sqrt{\\frac{3+2x}{x-1}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Use your answer to part a) to write a recurrence relation for finding a solution to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then starting with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, find a solution to 4 decimal places.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x^3-x^2-2x-3=x^2(x-1)-2x-3=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x^2(x-1)=3+2x\\Rightarrow x^2=\\frac{3+2x}{x-1}\\Rightarrow x=\\sqrt{\\frac{3+2x}{x-1}}\\text{ as req.}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=\\sqrt{\\frac{3-2x_n}{x_n-1}}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_2=2.645751311\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_3=2.2445777041\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Solution is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2.3744\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to 4 decimal places.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.28-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=x^2\\ln x-5x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has a solution between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Show that the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> may be written in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\sqrt{\\frac{5x}{\\ln x}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Use your answer to part b) to write a recurrence relation for finding a solution to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then starting with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, find a solution to 4 decimal places.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(3)=-5.112489402\\ldots&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(4)=2.180709778\\ldots&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is continuous and there is a change of sign then there is a solution between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2\\ln x=5x\\Rightarrow x^2=\\frac{5x}{\\ln x}\\Rightarrow x=\\sqrt{\\frac{5x}{\\ln x}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=\\sqrt{\\frac{5x_n}{\\ln(x_n)}}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_2=3.695076237\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_3=3.759747791\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Solution is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=3.7687\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to 4 decimal places.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.28-q5","number":5,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q5 b): Radians</strong> For each of the following recurrence relations, find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> giving your answer to 4 decimal places:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=\\sqrt{x_n+3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=2\\sin(x_n)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is measured in radians)</p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=8-\\frac1{10}e^{0.4x_n}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=0.1x_n^3-0.5x_n+2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_2=2.8284\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_3=2.4142\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_4=2.3268\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_2=1.6829\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_3=1.9874\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_4=1.8289\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_2=7.9000\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_3=5.6429\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_4=7.0444\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_2=1.8000\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_3=1.6832\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_4=1.6353\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.28-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>For each graph below, draw a diagram to show the convergence or divergence cobweb or staircase starting at the indicated point, labelling each of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><p>Identify whether it is a convergent or a divergent cobweb or staircase diagram.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.28/questions/assets/diagrams/228-q6a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.28/questions/assets/diagrams/228-q6b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.28/questions/assets/diagrams/228-q6c.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.28/questions/assets/diagrams/228-q6d.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.28/solutions/assets/diagrams/228-s6a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.28/solutions/assets/diagrams/228-s6b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.28/solutions/assets/diagrams/228-s6c.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.28/solutions/assets/diagrams/228-s6d.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.28-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>The diagram shows <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2x^2-1.5x+0.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on the same graph. They intersect when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac14\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.28/questions/assets/diagrams/228-q7.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>Describe what happens in terms of a cobweb or staircase diagram for each of the following starting points:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac14&lt;x_1&lt;\\frac14\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=\\frac14\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac14&lt;x_1&lt;1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1&gt;1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>It will staircase and then cobweb to the intersection at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac14\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>It directly gives the intersection at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac14\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>It will cobweb or staircase/cobweb to the intersection at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac14\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>It directly gives the intersection at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p>It diverges away (as a staircase) from the solution at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.28-q8","number":8,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q8 b): Radians</strong> Each of the following iterative formulae has a sequence which converges to a limit <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\alpha\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. In each case, deduce an interval of width 0.001 in which <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\" data-display=\"false\"></span> lies:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=2+\\ln x_n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=\\cos^2(x_n)+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=1.15\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is measured in radians)</p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=\\frac32x_n-\\frac1{10}x_n^4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{array}{c|l}n&amp;x_n\\\\\\hline2&amp;3.098612289\\ldots\\\\3&amp;3.130954362\\ldots\\\\4&amp;3.141337866\\ldots\\\\5&amp;3.144648781\\ldots\\\\6&amp;3.145702209\\ldots\\\\7&amp;3.146037143\\ldots\\\\8&amp;3.146143611\\ldots\\end{array}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\\in[3.146,3.147]\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{array}{c|l}n&amp;x_n\\\\\\hline2&amp;1.16861989\\ldots\\\\3&amp;1.154479721\\ldots\\\\4&amp;1.163534853\\ldots\\\\5&amp;1.156892261\\ldots\\\\6&amp;1.161754207\\ldots\\\\7&amp;1.158189672\\ldots\\\\8&amp;1.160799868\\ldots\\\\9&amp;1.158886807\\ldots\\\\10&amp;1.160288018\\ldots\\\\11&amp;1.159261221\\ldots\\\\12&amp;1.160013389\\ldots\\\\13&amp;1.159462256\\ldots\\end{array}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\\in[1.159,1.160]\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{array}{c|l}n&amp;x_n\\\\\\hline2&amp;1.4\\\\3&amp;1.71584\\\\4&amp;1.706983453\\ldots\\\\5&amp;1.711456501\\ldots\\\\6&amp;1.709231821\\ldots\\\\7&amp;1.710347038\\ldots\\\\8&amp;1.709790159\\ldots\\\\9&amp;1.71006878\\ldots\\end{array}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\\in[1.709,1.710]\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.28-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>An iterative formula for finding root <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=\\mathrm g(x_n)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. By considering <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g'(\\alpha)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in each of the following cases, explain whether the iterative formula will converge or diverge to the given root (given to 3 decimal places) from a point considered close to the root.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=x_n^5-2x_n^4-5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha=2.273\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=e^{x_n}-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha=1.146\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=e^{x_n}-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha=-1.841\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g(x)=x^5-2x^4-5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g'(x)=5x^4-8x^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g'(2.273)=5(2.273)^4-8(2.273)^3=39.51&gt;1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So it diverges from the root.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g(x)=e^x-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g'(x)=e^x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g'(1.146)=e^{1.146}=3.146&gt;1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so it diverges from the root.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g(x)=e^x-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g'(x)=e^x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g'(-1.841)=e^{-1.841}=0.1587&lt;1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so it converges to the root.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.28-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>Harry is trying to find the values of the three roots of the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^3-3x^2-x+4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. He rearranges the equation into four of the possible iterative formula <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=\\mathrm g(x_n)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to find a solution <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, including finding an initial point:</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm A:\\quad x_{n+1}&amp;=x_n^3-3x_n^2+4 &amp; x_1&amp;=2\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm B:\\quad x_{n+1}&amp;=\\sqrt[3]{3x_n^2+x_n-4} &amp; x_1&amp;=2.8\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm C:\\quad x_{n+1}&amp;=\\frac{x_n-4}{x_n^2-3x_n} &amp; x_1&amp;=1.2\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm D:\\quad x_{n+1}&amp;=-\\sqrt{\\frac{x_n^3-x_n+4}3} &amp; x_1&amp;=-1\n\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the three roots using the iterative formulae B, C and D at the given initial points above, giving your answers to 2 decimal places.</p></li><li><p>By considering <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g'(\\alpha)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on iterative formula A, explain why this iterative process does not converge to a root for each of the roots that you found in part a).</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Iterative formula B: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_2=2.815559633\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_3=2.827187864\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_4=2.835855288\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2.86\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (2 DP).</p>","<p>Iterative formula C: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_2=1.296296296\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_3=1.224223602\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_4=1.276836976\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1.25\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (2 DP).</p>","<p>Iterative formula D: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_2=-1.154700538\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_3=-1.097740076\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_4=-1.121743696\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1.11\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (2 DP).</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g(x)=x^3-3x^2-x+4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g'(x)=3x^2-6x-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g'(2.86)=6.3788&gt;1,\\quad\\mathrm g'(1.25)=-3.8125&lt;-1,\\quad\\mathrm g'(-1.11)=9.3563&gt;1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Convergence requires <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-1&lt;\\mathrm g'(\\alpha)&lt;1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which does not hold for any of the roots.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.28-q11","number":11,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch the graphs <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac1x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sin x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to show that the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1x=\\sin x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has exactly one solution for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;x&lt;\\frac\\pi2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Show that the solution to the equation lies between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>By using a suitable iterative formula, obtain an approximation solution to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1x=\\sin x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to 4 decimal places.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.28/solutions/assets/diagrams/228-s11a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\frac1x-\\sin x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(1)=\\tfrac11-\\sin1=0.1585&gt;0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(1.2)=\\tfrac11-\\sin1=-0.0987&lt;0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is continuous and there is a change of sign between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> therefore there is a solution to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1x=\\sin x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=\\frac1{\\sin(x_n)}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_2=1.188395106\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_3=1.07785184\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_4=1.35146857\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The solution is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1.1142\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to (4 DP).</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.28-q12","number":12,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch the graphs <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=e^{x-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2+\\ln x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on the same axes, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;x&lt;4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Explain why the solutions to the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=e^{x-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are also solutions to the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"e^{x-2}=2+\\ln x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.28/solutions/assets/diagrams/228-s12a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>All3 graphs intercept at the same points.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.28-q13","number":13,"question":"<p>The number of tickets sold <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"N\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for an event in the first 48 hours of sales is modelled by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"N=3t-e^{0.1t}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the time in hours passed. When the number of tickets sold drops to zero and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=T\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> satisfies <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=10\\ln(3T)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Write a recurrence relation to find the solutions to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=10\\ln(3T)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and starting with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_1=48\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, find a solution to the equation to 3 decimal places.</p></li><li><p>Hence state the number of hours that have passed, to the nearest hour, when the number of tickets being sold is zero.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0=3T-e^{0.1T}\\Rightarrow0.1T=\\ln(3T)\\Rightarrow T=10\\ln(3T)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_{n+1}=10\\ln(3T_n)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_2=49.698133\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_3=50.04579656\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_3=50.11550806\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=50.133\" data-display=\"false\"></span> hours.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>50 hours</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.28-q14","number":14,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q14: Radians</strong></p><p>A circle with centre O has a chord such that the angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AOB=\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> radians where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;\\theta&lt;\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.28/questions/assets/diagrams/228-q14.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The area of the segment cut off by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac16\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of the area of the circle.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta-\\sin\\theta=\\frac\\pi3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol><p>The solution lies between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><p>Using an iterative method, find the solution correct to 2 decimal places.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Segment: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12r^2\\theta-\\frac{r^2}2\\sin\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\tfrac16\\pi r^2=\\tfrac12r^2\\theta-\\tfrac{r^2}2\\sin\\theta\\Rightarrow\\tfrac16\\pi=\\tfrac12\\theta-\\tfrac12\\sin\\theta\\Rightarrow\\tfrac\\pi3=\\theta-\\sin\\theta\\text{ as req.}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\tfrac\\pi3=\\theta-\\sin\\theta\\Rightarrow\\theta=\\sin\\theta+\\tfrac\\pi3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta_{n+1}=\\sin\\theta_n+\\frac\\pi3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta_1=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta_2=1.956494978\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta_3=1.9737333373\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta_4=1.967110835\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta=1.97\" data-display=\"false\"></span> radians (2 DP).</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.28-q15","number":15,"question":"<p>Giving your answers to 3 decimal places, use an iterative method to find the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-coordinates of the points of intersection of:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\cos x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\\log_3(0.5x+1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\cos x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=\\cos(x_n)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=0.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_2=0.8775825619\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_3=0.6390124942\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_4=0.8026851007\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0.739\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 DP).</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x^2=x\\log_3(0.5x+1)\\Rightarrow x^2-x\\log_3(0.5x+1)=0\\Rightarrow x(x-\\log_3(0.5x+1))=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x-\\log_3(0.5x+1)=0\\Rightarrow x=\\log_3(0.5x+1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=\\log_3(0.5x_n+1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> DIVERGES.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3^x=0.5x+1\\Rightarrow3^x-1=0.5x\\Rightarrow x=2\\times3^x-2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_2=-1.333333333\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_3=-1.53775915\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_4=-1.630739868\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1.686\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 DP).</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.28-q16","number":16,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q16: Inverse Trigonometric Functions</strong></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch the graphs of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3\\arctan(2x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on the same axes for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-4\\leq x\\leq4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Show that there is a solution to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2-3\\arctan(2x)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1.8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>By using a suitable iterative formula, obtain an approximation solution to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2-3\\arctan(2x)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to 3 decimal places.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.28/solutions/assets/diagrams/228-s16a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=x^2-3\\arctan(2x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(1.8)=1.8^2-3\\arctan(3.6)=-0.6595\\ldots&lt;0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(2.2)=2.2^2-3\\arctan(4.4)=0.7980\\ldots&gt;0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is continuous and there is a change in sign between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1.8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> there must be a root.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=\\sqrt{3\\arctan(2x_n)}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_2=1.994355282\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_3=1.993854416\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_4=1.993809838\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_5=1.99380587\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1.994\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 DP).</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.28-q17","number":17,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q17: Differentiation of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\ln x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></strong> The diagram shows the graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac{2x^2+24}{3\\sqrt x}-4\\ln x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The stationary point of the curve is labelled <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.28/questions/assets/diagrams/228-q17.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> satisfies <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0=\\sqrt x-\\frac14x^2\\sqrt x-x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Use the iteration formula <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=\\sqrt{x_n}-\\frac14x_n^2\\sqrt{x_n}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> starting at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to find the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-coordinate of point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to 2 decimal places.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac{2x^2+24}{3\\sqrt x}-4\\ln x=-\\tfrac23x^{3/2}-8x^{-1/2}-4\\ln x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=-x^{1/2}+4x^{-3/2}-\\frac4x=-\\sqrt x+\\frac4{x\\sqrt x}-\\frac4x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Stat pt when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-\\sqrt x+\\frac4{x\\sqrt x}-\\frac4x=0\\Rightarrow-x^2+4-4\\sqrt x=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-x^2\\sqrt x+4\\sqrt x-4x=0\\Rightarrow-\\tfrac14x^2\\sqrt x+\\sqrt x-x=0\\text{ as req.}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=\\sqrt{x_n}-\\frac14x_n^2\\sqrt{x_n}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=1.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_2=0.75\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_3=0.7442405814\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_4=0.7432335552\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0.74\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (2 DP).</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.28-q18","number":18,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q18: Double Angle Formulae</strong> An approximate solution to an equation can be found using the iterative formula <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=\\frac14\\arccos x_n\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>By using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=0.3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> giving your answers to 4 decimal places.</p></li><li><p>Show that the iterative formula may be used to find a solution to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x-1+8\\sin^2x\\cos^2x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_2=0.3165\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (4 DP), <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_3=0.3122\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (4 DP), <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_4=0.3133\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (4 DP)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x=\\tfrac14\\arccos x\\Rightarrow4x=\\arccos x\\Rightarrow\\cos(4x)=x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Use double angle formula:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x=1-2\\sin^2(2x)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Use of double angle formula:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x=1-2(2\\sin x\\cos x)^2\\Rightarrow x=1-8\\sin^2x\\cos^2x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x-1+8\\sin^2x\\cos^2x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>"]}]